{
  "slug": "officecli",
  "name": "Officecli",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "OfficeCLI is a Claude Code plugin for local Office document workflows. It helps Claude create, update, and convert Office files when the local OfficeCLI installation supports the requested task.\n\nThe plugin is intended for workflows such as:\n\n- creating PowerPoint presentations in pptx\n- creating Word documents in docx\n- creating structured worksheets in xlsx\n- checking whether a requested Office workflow is supported before execution\n\nThe plugin packages a Claude Code skill and routes supported Office-file tasks to the user's local officecli installation. It is designed for users who want Claude-assisted Office document workflows while keeping execution on their own\nmachine.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill**, `officecli` (Use when the task involves Office document or standalone image handling such as creating, modifying, or converting PPTX,…).\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install officecli@claude-community` from `officecli/officecli-skills` (`plugins/officecli`).",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "antigravity",
    "codex"
  ],
